{# --- Document order (W3C SCXML 3.13) ------------------------------------

   Transitions are emitted in the order the author wrote them, and `when`
   takes the first branch that matches, so the two orders agree by
   construction rather than by a sort.

   ⚠ A bare wildcard used to be pre-scanned OUT of this loop and emitted as
   the `else` branch wherever it sat, which placed it after transitions
   written after it. Measured 2026-09-13 by
   `integration_resources/event_descriptor_spellings_agree/`: a state whose
   `.*` was written first took the literal transition written second.

   An UNGUARDED wildcard still becomes `else`. It matches every event this
   function can be called with — eventless transitions are dispatched by
   `processNullEvent` and never reach here — so nothing written after it is
   reachable, and `ns.sealed` both stops the loop and drops those dead
   branches. A GUARDED wildcard is a branch like any other: when its guard is
   false the transitions after it ARE reachable, so it is emitted in place
   with its own condition instead of being hoisted to the end. #}
{% set ns = namespace(sealed=false, seal_trans=none) %}

